outputs.exact_statement:
The map $\Phi_{p,a}$ and the positive function $f_{p,a}$ are smooth on $M$. For every $X\in T_xM$, $$\label{eq:map-comparison}
 \begin{aligned}
 |d\Phi_{p,a}(X)|&\le f_{p,a}|X|,\\
 \mathop{\mathrm{Hess}}u_{p,a}&\le du_{p,a}\otimes du_{p,a}
 -\frac12\bigl(b^2+f_{p,a}^2+|\nabla u_{p,a}|^2\bigr)g.
 \end{aligned}$$ The second inequality is one of quadratic forms. The functions depend smoothly on $(p,a,x)$. For fixed $o\in M$, parallel transport of the first component of $\Phi_{p,a}$ from $p$ to $o$ along the unique geodesic also depends smoothly on $(p,a,x)$.

Let $(M^n,g)$ be complete and simply connected with $\mathop{\mathrm{sec}}_g\le0$. For $p\in M$, write $\log_p=\exp_p^{-1}$, $r_p(x)=d(p,x)$, and $D_p=r_p^2/2$. Then $$\label{eq:distance-metric-comparison}
 \mathop{\mathrm{Hess}}_gD_p\ge g,\qquad (\exp_p)^*g\ge g_p,
 \qquad |d\log_p(X)|_{g_p}\le |X|_g.$$ Here $g_p$ on $T_pM$ denotes its constant Euclidean metric.

For every Lipschitz function $v$ with compact support in $\Sigma^\circ$, $$\label{eq:extrinsic-sobolev}
 Q_\Sigma(v)\ge
 Y_m\left(\int_\Sigma |v|^q\,d\sigma\right)^{2/q}.$$ The inequality also holds for the zero extension of every $v\in H^1_0(U)$, where $U\Subset\Sigma^\circ$ is open.

Let $F:M\to M$ be an orientation-preserving smooth diffeomorphism, and let $E$ have finite perimeter. If the right side below is finite, then $$\label{eq:bv-flow-jacobian}
 P(FE)=\int_{\partial^*E}
 J_{n-1}\bigl(dF_x|_{N_E(x)^\perp}\bigr)\,d\mathcal H_g^{n-1}(x).$$ All Jacobians and adjoints use the source and target Riemannian metrics. For a smooth flow $F_t$ with velocity $Z$ and a set whose perimeter support is compact, $$\label{eq:bv-flow-first-variation}
 \left.\frac d{dt}\right|_{t=0}P(F_tE)
 =\int_{\partial^*E}\mathop{\mathrm{div}}_{N_E^\perp}Z\,d\mathcal H_g^{n-1}.$$ For a fixed finite family of flows and perimeter supports contained in a fixed compact set, there are common $C,\tau>0$ such that $|P(F_tE)-P(E)|\le C|t|P(E)$ for $|t|<\tau$.

Let $0<v<\mathop{\mathrm{Vol}}(B)$, and let $E$ be a confined minimizing region of volume $v$. There are constants $C<\infty$ and $r_0>0$, depending on $E$ and $B$, such that $$\label{eq:singular-area-growth}
 \sigma\bigl(\Sigma\cap B_r(x)\bigr)\le Cr^m
 \qquad(x\in S,\ 0<r<r_0).$$

Let $v\in(0,\mathop{\mathrm{Vol}}(B))$ be a differentiability point of $I$, and let $E$ minimize the confined perimeter at volume $v$. Then $$\label{eq:constant-sobolev}
 m\int_\Sigma(h^2-b^2)\,d\sigma
 \ge Y_m I(v)^{(m-2)/m}.$$
